# .gitleaksignore — the committed synthetic fixtures the secret scan may skip.
#
# One fingerprint per line, `<path>:<rule-id>:<line>` (the shape gitleaks emits
# for `detect --no-git`). gitleaks reads this file from the scan root whatever
# `--config` it was given, so it is the ONE list that silences the CI review
# action's scan (which pins its own config) AND a local `gitleaks detect`;
# .gitleaks.toml's path allowlist reaches local runs only. Every entry below is
# a value that authenticates nothing — the same bar as `secrets.scanExempt` in
# the crates' guardrails.config.json: extending this file requires proving the
# value is not a real credential. Fingerprints are line-anchored, so an edit
# that moves a flagged line brings the finding back until the entry is updated;
# scripts/test/gitleaks_ignore_test.sh fails when an entry no longer points at
# an existing line, and refuses any path outside a tests/ tree.

# `MIIphony`: a PEM-shaped dummy with no key material, used to exercise the
# PEM parser's error path and the secret masker.
crates/config/tests/app_store_test.rs:private-key:15
crates/shared/tests/secret_masker_test.rs:private-key:218

# A 2048-bit key generated with `openssl genrsa` for the #201 App-JWT tests and
# never uploaded to any GitHub App (AGENTS.md): it signs test JWTs that no
# server accepts.
crates/protocol/tests/fixtures/app_jwt_test_key.pem:private-key:1

